$G$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[G\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:=-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{G}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c56b3e9-cf23-5e1e-8c7d-c474059c9a9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d12939ef-7783-5366-8c5e-2d0057653114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335638} {:answer/id #uuid "308e402d-6c05-5859-a221-cd91990a1a80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{8} & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335639} {:answer/id #uuid "08e007af-34b5-5fb5-8bfb-b9f37e0b94e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335640} {:answer/id #uuid "2e86e596-10ab-51ad-8af2-66fc0adbf441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335641} {:answer/id #uuid "8f25d323-0dba-5482-8b1b-d63e824aa0d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{8} & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08e007af-34b5-5fb5-8bfb-b9f37e0b94e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335640} :answer-field/id #uuid "a30c62f5-2915-54b2-911e-75cc57578756" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b534169a-9dbf-54bd-873e-e260f6c5b586" :question/math-academy-id "q-73646" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$K=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $K$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{K}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335643 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1172f0d-3100-59db-a4a7-83423cce999f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335645} {:answer/id #uuid "1817ffa4-e84b-518d-b7d0-59e24f3f3d1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335646} {:answer/id #uuid "5019d738-a8c5-5f3a-8b09-880f5e5960bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335647} {:answer/id #uuid "b618fa54-c2d8-5d8c-97b3-3e9fa8786624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335648} {:answer/id #uuid "248e9333-4f3b-5911-8bc2-79e052106f8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1172f0d-3100-59db-a4a7-83423cce999f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335645} :answer-field/id #uuid "01f4020a-dcba-5680-86e1-71984b3e0774" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd74f139-452a-58af-a7f9-3d3621835dfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-73647" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{2}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335650 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2466f75a-6305-5af3-b476-957171788c60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335652} {:answer/id #uuid "028df1de-8591-5a11-9974-87c12d27c0b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335653} {:answer/id #uuid "347e20c5-3736-5d9d-b23b-7d33652934bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335654} {:answer/id #uuid "3304334f-8b4a-5903-8d3a-9fd522579dac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335655} {:answer/id #uuid "5a99db91-30a7-539c-a388-51f1ea62ce71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "028df1de-8591-5a11-9974-87c12d27c0b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335653} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bc4336d-0944-5804-92f5-eddebf454871" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "901d7bdd-b877-50eb-b32d-27ea08b5103b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73651" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{2}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62363135-995f-5aa7-93e7-8e2940c26133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335659} {:answer/id #uuid "40b2a47e-7f26-5454-936d-bd6a4871c749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335660} {:answer/id #uuid "065152d1-7e00-5b59-95d4-7122f09285db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335661} {:answer/id #uuid "91fd9ef1-c244-5a34-8dde-fbe3052ba5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335662} {:answer/id #uuid "cf4f1c53-fa8b-5497-90ea-d04ff95daad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40b2a47e-7f26-5454-936d-bd6a4871c749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335660} :answer-field/id #uuid "0467fafd-c59e-52bf-81d9-b98499143b21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "71966071-c211-51cd-afce-1e8a23d5fd0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73680" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{E}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{2}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}]}
